# PR Size And Stack

## Limit

Implementation lines per pull request must stay around 400 or below. Beyond that, split the work into a coherent stack of dependent PRs.

## Implementation Lines Defined

"Implementation" means production code in the PR's primary layer. The size budget excludes:

- Tests (`**/*.test.*`, `**/*.spec.*`, `**/__tests__/**`, `**/__mocks__/**`)
- Fixtures (`**/fixtures/**`)
- Snapshots and generated files (`**/*.generated.*`, `**/__snapshots__/**`)
- API test collections (Bruno/Postman/Insomnia folders)
- Markdown, JSON, YAML, and other config files

Tests-only or docs-only PRs do not trigger the limit, but should still be split when reviewability suffers.

## Measurement

Always use `gh` or the GitHub MCP. Raw `git` CLI commands are forbidden in this workflow.

```bash
gh pr view <PR_NUMBER> --json files --jq '.files[] | "\(.additions)\t\(.deletions)\t\(.path)"'
```

Filter the returned file metadata to the implementation files defined above and sum the `additions` values. Without an open PR, estimate from the changed files; if estimation is uncertain, ask the user.

## Stack Rules

- Each PR in the stack must be reviewable on its own.
- Stacks may have sequential dependencies. Circular dependencies are forbidden.
- Stacks should not introduce flaky behavior between merges.
- The first PR in the stack lands the foundation (types, contracts); later PRs land consumers.

## Validation

Operationally enforced by `.cursor/skills/pr-readiness-check/SKILL.md` (size + iteration loop with external feedback).

Pair with `.cursor/rules/process/one-layer-per-pr.mdc` and `.cursor/rules/process/source-of-truth.mdc`.
